e  arm I know I know  say good night to mr. Hameed and thank  you for dinner thank you for dinner mr.  Hamid soldier smiles at him good night  little soldier she guides Sammy away by  the beam of the light interior Sammy's  room continuous she tucks him under his  blanket and hands him the flashlight  don't waste the battery okay okay will  you feed the kitty  yeah I'll feed kidding okay I miss Bubba  me too my love every time I pray I ask  Allah to bring him home me too okay  Allah is watching over us  remember that good night good night mama  she turns off his flashlight leaves his  door slightly ajar interior Freitas  apartment dining area continuous Frieda  sits back at the table across from  soldier I can tell you're a caring  mother thank you  loving your child isn't hard it's  natural yes instinct she sips her water  then looks over at the sniper rifle  leaning against the wall I could never  do what you do he thinks for a moment no  one was born a killer we only fight  because we have to he stares at her  maybe we're not so different  you know you and I she looks at him not  sure she agrees but unwilling to  challenge him I don't know rather it's  instinct or destiny but I know it's his  will it seems to me our instincts often  go against his will but how could I know  for sure he shrugs here's what I can  tell you when it's your life or theirs  the act is simple you raised the barrel  resting it on your arm listening or the  window sill just like this focus the  scope finding your target in the  crosshairs and you hold the butt tight  but guess your cheek to move with the  recoil exhale deeply so your breathing  doesn't move the barrel and when all  your breath has left your body and not  one ounce remains pull the trigger  physics does the rest she looks at him  his eyes only seem colder in the dim  light he puts his arms down something  changes in you you know it can never be  undone when you accept this it becomes  easier she looks at him suddenly aware 